(The indoor court where the Tennis Court Oath was sworn in 1789, igniting the French Revolution.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 669.6484251968503258 Td
(The Jeu de Paume, built in 1686 by Jules Hardouin-Mansart, is an indoor court for the game of 'jeu de paume' — an) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 657.7996062992125417 Td
(early form of tennis that was wildly popular at the court of Versailles. The building is a long, narrow hall with high) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 645.9507874015747575 Td
(windows and a vaulted ceiling, designed to provide the specific acoustics and lighting required for the sport.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 622.2531496062991891 Td
(Louis XIV was an avid player, and the Jeu de Paume at Versailles was one of the finest in France. The king played) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 610.4043307086612913 Td
(regularly, and the court was also used for tournaments that drew the best players in the country. The sport was so) Tj
