/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 598.5555118110235071 Td
(popular that the term 'devoir de paume' — the obligation to play tennis — was a recognized part of court life.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 574.8578740157479388 Td
(But the Jeu de Paume's historical significance far transcends sport. On June 20, 1789, the deputies of the Third Estate,) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 563.0090551181101546 Td
(locked out of their regular meeting place, assembled in the Jeu de Paume and took the famous Tennis Court Oath,) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 551.1602362204722567 Td
(pledging not to disband until they had written a constitution for France. This moment is widely regarded as the birth of) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 539.3114173228344725 Td
(the French Revolution and the end of absolute monarchy.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 515.6137795275587905 Td
(Today, the Jeu de Paume houses a museum dedicated to the Revolution. The empty hall, with its simple architecture and) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 503.7649606299210063 Td
(profound historical resonance, is one of the most moving spaces at Versailles. A painting by Jacques-Louis David,) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.235 g
56.6929133858267775 491.9161417322831653 Td
(commemorating the Tennis Court Oath, dominates one wall — though it was never completed, its unfinished state adds) Tj
